# Logic Change Checklist

Use this checklist for every correctness/completeness change that affects runtime logic.

## Inputs and Contracts

- Identify the upstream contract being changed (`host_data.type/event`, API payload, migration SQL, cache key, or plot schema).
- Document the canonical source for that contract (monitor schema, analysis catalog, serializer, or compose config).
- Verify cross-layer name/priority consistency (analysis -> API -> frontend -> tests).

## Invariants

- Define expected invariants before and after change (idempotence, monotonic counters, bounded percentages, cache freshness).
- Verify non-staff/staff behavior and no-data fallbacks remain deterministic.
- Verify runtime config assumptions (`db`, `redis`, compose network aliases, required env vars).

## Failure Modes

- List at least one transient failure scenario (DB/Redis/network/cache write failure) and expected fallback.
- Confirm exceptions are logged with actionable context and do not silently corrupt behavior.
- Confirm retry and timeout behavior is bounded and configurable.

## Regression Tests

- Add or update targeted unit tests for changed logic.
- Add or update integration/E2E tests when route/UI/output behavior changes.
- For ingestion/metrics/caching changes, include stale-data and invalidation boundary tests.

## Validation Runbook

- Run smallest targeted test modules first.
- Run compose-backed validation for DB/Redis dependent paths.
- Record what passed, what was skipped, and residual risks.

## Overlap

- **`implementation-review-workflow.mdc`** — general plan-before-code and post-implementation self-review; use this checklist when runtime logic changes.
- Complements `runtime-resource-and-metrics-safety.mdc`, `bugfix-and-perf-change-playbook.mdc`, and test-maintenance rules.
